From 767f2ec2054bc90353d16ea350ab55be985a56fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 04:16:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Trade journal, pattern recognition, corporate filings, and
 live-site fixes

Trade journal
- Entries stored in the viewer's browser only, never uploaded, never in the
  repo. Plotted on the chart as buy/sell arrows beside the news markers.
- Net position with average cost and realised/unrealised P&L against the
  live price, plus JSON export and import.
- Gate ships as a PBKDF2-SHA256 derivation in config/auth.json (310k
  iterations) so the published page stays shut without the password ever
  entering the repository. It stops visitors; it is not security, and it
  guards nothing valuable because the entries never leave the browser.

Pattern recognition
- Candlestick patterns (engulfing, hammer, shooting star, doji, morning and
  evening star, three soldiers and crows, gaps) and chart structures (double
  top and bottom, head and shoulders both ways, ascending and descending
  triangles). Thresholds in ATR so one rule set covers 1m to 1w candles.
- Every pattern is measured against its own prior occurrences in the loaded
  history and labelled with what actually happened, e.g. "BE 58%" of 136.
  Under 8 occurrences is flagged thin and demoted. A doji claims indecision
  so it reports an up-rate and no hit rate. On random-walk data the rates
  land near 50%, confirming the statistic does not manufacture edge.

Corporate filings and social
- scripts/fetch_filings.py pulls BSE and NSE announcements and scores them by
  materiality, heaviest category winning so an NCLT order reads as distress
  rather than an order win. Merged into the news store with a Filings filter.
- Reddit and YouTube RSS added to the feed index, now 442 feeds.

Live-site fixes found by loading the deployed page
- The forecast panel was display:none below 1080px, so a laptop showed a
  chart and no forecast. It now sits under the chart instead of vanishing.
- impact_high held bare institution words, tagging 45% of headlines HIGH.
  Impact now needs corroboration and procedural notices are downgraded; on
  the live 600-item feed this moves HIGH from 270 to 103.
- RBI press releases flooded the stream by sharing one timestamp. Display
  holds back an over-represented source, max 3 in a row; distinct sources in
  the visible list went from a handful to 42.
- Removed the browser-side proxied RSS lane: jina rate-limits and strips the
  XML, allorigins refused, rss2json errored. Breadth is the workflow's job.

